WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.400
Radial glial fibres guide young neurons outward.

2
00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:09.580
Are those same cells also the source of the neurons?

3
00:00:10.633 --> 00:00:15.393
In 1972, Pasko Rakic studied fetal rhesus monkey cortex.

4
00:00:16.353 --> 00:00:18.873
He found young neurons pressed against radial fibres.

5
00:00:20.017 --> 00:00:22.757
Radial glia were seen mainly as scaffolds.

6
00:00:23.537 --> 00:00:27.217
Neurons, it was thought, came from some other cell in the ventricular zone.

7
00:00:28.267 --> 00:00:33.187
Around the year 2000, three lines of evidence in rodents, using four methods,

8
00:00:33.187 --> 00:00:34.327
changed the picture.

9
00:00:35.207 --> 00:00:36.967
Each asked the question a different way.

10
00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:42.370
For each one, ask: if radial glia were only a scaffold, what would we see?

11
00:00:43.333 --> 00:00:44.873
First, sorting, in mouse.

12
00:00:45.733 --> 00:00:50.273
The Götz group used mice that make GFP from a human GFAP promoter.

13
00:00:51.417 --> 00:00:54.817
Rodent radial glia make little GFAP protein.

14
00:00:55.337 --> 00:00:58.397
But that human promoter fragment is active in them.

15
00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:01.570
The green cells were sorted into a dish.

16
00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:05.650
If they were only scaffolds, you might expect few or no neurons.

17
00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:07.610
Did they make any?

18
00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:15.100
In culture, they made neurons.

19
00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:17.780
But a dish shows potential, not fate.

20
00:01:18.783 --> 00:01:21.043
Second, fate mapping in the living mouse.

21
00:01:21.923 --> 00:01:26.243
An enzyme called Cre recombinase was made from a GFAP promoter.

22
00:01:27.367 --> 00:01:30.647
Cre cuts out a stop sequence in front of a reporter gene.

23
00:01:31.447 --> 00:01:33.047
The cut is a change in the DNA.

24
00:01:34.133 --> 00:01:38.913
So it is copied into every descendant, even after the promoter switches off in a

25
00:01:38.913 --> 00:01:39.913
neuron.

26
00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:44.473
If radial glia were only scaffolds, cortical neurons would stay dark.

27
00:01:45.313 --> 00:01:46.353
What did the fate map show?

28
00:01:52.333 --> 00:01:55.953
Nearly all cortical projection neurons carried the reporter.

29
00:01:57.013 --> 00:02:00.013
Cortical interneurons, local inhibitory cells, did not.

30
00:02:00.913 --> 00:02:02.593
They are born in the ventral forebrain.

31
00:02:03.567 --> 00:02:05.527
Third, filming lineage, in rat.

32
00:02:06.327 --> 00:02:10.387
A retrovirus carrying GFP was injected into the ventricles.

33
00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:16.530
This retrovirus enters only dividing cells, and these cells divide right at the

34
00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:20.330
ventricle. Every descendant of a marked cell inherits the mark.

35
00:02:21.283 --> 00:02:24.643
A green radial glial cell divides at the ventricle.

36
00:02:25.263 --> 00:02:26.263
It keeps its fibre.

37
00:02:27.233 --> 00:02:30.893
Its daughter becomes a neuron and moves out along a parental fibre.

38
00:02:31.833 --> 00:02:36.013
In mouse, Miyata and colleagues saw a newborn neuron inherit the fibre itself.

39
00:02:37.067 --> 00:02:38.867
Last, recording, in rat.

40
00:02:39.487 --> 00:02:43.047
Precursors were recorded with an electrode, then filled with dye.

41
00:02:44.067 --> 00:02:46.687
The filled cells had the shape of radial glia.

42
00:02:47.647 --> 00:02:52.187
Radial glial markers labeled nearly all cells caught in S phase or mitosis.

43
00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:54.990
Each method has a blind spot.

44
00:02:55.930 --> 00:02:56.950
A dish shows potential.

45
00:02:57.650 --> 00:03:00.150
An electrode samples only cells it can reach.

46
00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:02.690
A marker is not a family tree.

47
00:03:03.683 --> 00:03:05.203
But the blind spots differ.

48
00:03:06.103 --> 00:03:08.803
And every result went against a scaffold-only view.

49
00:03:09.643 --> 00:03:12.783
The fate map and the films showed neuronal ancestry directly.

50
00:03:13.917 --> 00:03:19.737
So in embryonic rodent cortex, the cell that guides migrating neurons is also the

51
00:03:19.737 --> 00:03:20.997
cell that makes most of them.
